Z||000000||Fret Naught||04-27-2000||12:44 PM||||Does any one have input about leather seat kits? I see that Mr. Mikes has a lot to offer, and I am thinking of buying his kits.<P>They seem reasonable in price. Looking for input Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||04-27-2000||12:51 PM||||I saw Mr. Mike's seats while I was at Daytona a couple of years ago.  They look great.  I'd like to swap out mine after I get my three daughters out of college.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||04-27-2000||01:33 PM||||Mr. Mike has some of the nicest leather reupolstry material.  From those I know who have used his kits they are relatively easy to install and look great.<P>Phil used another vendors leather reupolstry kit for his S/C 3800 coupe and his looked nice.  Phil you can chime in here and tell us the scoop on your seats.<P>I'm waiting to get lucky in a show door prize drawing to get a $200 gift certificate from Mr Mike so that I can get one of his kits.||||reg||10
Z||000003||Oreif||04-27-2000||02:24 PM||||I have a set of Mr. Mikes Seats. They were very easy to install. They look great and feel very comfortable! Takes about an hour per seat. He includes everything to do the job. Leather seats, hogrings, foam, hog ring tools, spray glue, and a very well done video on removing the old and installing new!<BR>Here is a quick pic of mine, I'll try to get a better pic of the whole seat.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image09_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000004||86 SE||04-27-2000||05:10 PM||||hey <BR>how much were the leather seats<P>they look grate too<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000005||Phil||04-27-2000||05:49 PM||||Whilst in Daytona I went out on the balcony of my hotel and started yakking with the guy in the next balcony. I was extolling the virtues of my Pisa leather seats and that I liked the design better than Mr. Mikes-he seemed very interested. Turns out it was Mr. Mike himself. He understood, we both got a good chuckle out of the whole thing.||||reg||1
